$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(mgdb-mgec
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
<meta name="twitter:site" content="@MaizeGDB">
<meta property="og:url" content="https://maizegdb.org/mgec">
<meta property="og:title" content="Maize Genetics Executive Committee | MaizeGDB">
<meta property="og:description" content="The record of the Maize Genetics Executive Committee, 2000 to 2019: its origins, procedures, elected committees, annual activity reports, and document archive.">

<a class="mgdb-skip-link" href="#mgec-main">Skip to main content</a>

<main class="mgdb-page mgdb-hub-page mgdb-mgec-page" id="mgec-main">

  <nav class="mgdb-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/maize_history">Community</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><span aria-current="page">MGEC</span>
  </nav>

  <section class="mgdb-hero" aria-labelledby="mgec-title">
    <div class="mgdb-hero-emblem">
      <svg class="mgec-hero-mark" viewBox="0 0 96 96" role="img" aria-label="A committee table">
        <circle cx="48" cy="52" r="26" fill="#e8f4ec" stroke="#235c37" stroke-width="3" />
        <g fill="#235c37">
          <circle cx="48" cy="18" r="7" /><circle cx="76" cy="30" r="7" /><circle cx="84" cy="60" r="7" />
          <circle cx="62" cy="84" r="7" /><circle cx="34" cy="84" r="7" /><circle cx="12" cy="60" r="7" />
          <circle cx="20" cy="30" r="7" />
        </g>
        <path d="M36 52h24M42 44h12M42 60h12" stroke="#d99a0b" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
      </svg>
      <strong>MGEC</strong>
      <span>2000 &#8211; 2019</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-hero-body">
      <h1 id="mgec-title">The Maize Genetics Executive Committee.</h1>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-description">For nineteen years an elected committee spoke for the maize genetics community to funding agencies, to growers, and to the wider life sciences. This is its record: $(term_count) terms of elected members, $(activity_count) annual activity reports, and the documents it produced.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mgdb-message mgdb-message-info mgec-archive-note" role="status">
    <div><strong>Archive notice.</strong> In 2019 the MGEC voted to establish a 501&#40;c&#41;&#40;3&#41;, the Maize Genetics Cooperation, and ceased its own activity. Current business is with the <a href="https://www.maizegenetics.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Maize Genetics Cooperation</a>. This page is the historical record and is no longer updated.</div>
  </div>

  <nav class="mgdb-section-tabs" aria-label="Sections on this page">
    <a href="#mgec-origins" class="is-current" aria-current="true">Origins</a>
    <a href="#mgec-procedures">Procedures</a>
    <a href="#mgec-activities">Activities</a>
    <a href="#mgec-committees">Committees</a>
    <a href="#mgec-documents">Documents</a>
    <a href="#mgec-related">Related resources</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="mgec-origins" aria-labelledby="mgec-origins-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="mgec-origins-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Origins</h2></div>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="mgec-mission">
      <p>It is the mission of the Maize Genetics Executive Committee to identify both the needs and the opportunities for maize genetics, and to communicate this information to the broadest possible life science community. This community includes scientists, funding sources for scientists, and the end users for the accomplishments of maize genetics, from farmers to consumers.</p>
      <cite>Jeff Bennetzen, <a href="http://mnl.maizegdb.org/mnl/75/mgec.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Maize Genetics Cooperation Newsletter 75</a></cite>
    </blockquote>

    <p class="mgec-lead">A brief history of organized communication in the maize genetics community, compiled by Jeff Bennetzen. For an extended history of the Cooperation and of the Stock Center prepared by Marty Sachs, see <a href="https://maizecoopsc.org/about" target="_blank" rel="noopener">maizecoopsc.org</a>.</p>

    <ol class="mgec-timeline">$(origin_rows)</ol>
  </section>

  <section id="mgec-procedures" aria-labelledby="mgec-procedures-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="mgec-procedures-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Procedures</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-prose mgec-prose">
      <h3>March 2004</h3>
      <p>The Maize Genetics Executive Committee will include ten members elected by the broadest feasible vote of the maize genetics community.</p>
      <p>Members will be elected for five-year terms. Two members will rotate off each year and will not be eligible for nomination for two succeeding years. Elections will take place in February of each year for any available seats, including the two that open each year and any that become available for other reasons. Nominations will be solicited from the entire maize genetics community, and all willing candidates will be present on the ballot. If there are more nominees than twice the number of open slots, a runoff ballot of twice the number of open slots will be conducted, for those nominees who receive the highest number of votes in the initial ballot. Elected candidates will be those with the most votes.</p>
      <p>To ensure broad representation, no more than two individuals from the same location or institution may serve on the MGEC simultaneously.</p>
      <p>The chair of the MGEC will be elected by a vote of the members of the MGEC.</p>
      <p>The MGEC has the option to appoint other members so that an appropriate representation of the maize genetics community will be obtained. These appointed positions will be filled via an election within the MGEC, and will be for a maximum of four years.</p>
      <p>Each year, the MGEC will report its activities to the maize genetics community via its web site and, if needed, by a short presentation at the annual Maize Genetics Conference.</p>

      <h3>Motions, March 23, 2018 &#8212; Saint-Malo, France</h3>
      <ol class="mgec-motions">
        <li>The PI of the Research Coordination Networks project can serve as an ex officio member of the MGEC.</li>
        <li>Ex officio member status does not carry voting rights. Appointed members of the MGEC have the right to vote.</li>
        <li>One can be an elected member of the MGEC and an ex officio member of the MGEC.</li>
        <li>The MaizeGDB representative is an ex officio member of the MGEC.</li>
        <li>If there are no elected members from industry on the MGEC, the MGEC may appoint one.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Motions, March 15, 2019 &#8212; St. Louis, Missouri</h3>
      <ol class="mgec-motions mgec-motions-alpha">
        <li>Motion to support David Jackson's nomination as vice chair.</li>
        <li>Motion to support the nomination of Eric Y. Danquah as the African representative.</li>
        <li>Motion to support the nomination of Sebastien Praud as the European representative.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="mgec-activities" aria-labelledby="mgec-activities-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="mgec-activities-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Activities</h2></div>
    </div>

    <p class="mgec-lead">What the committee reported doing, year by year. Each report was its own page until 2026; the years the committee did not publish a report are simply absent.</p>

    <div class="mgec-activities">$(activity_entries)</div>
  </section>

  <section id="mgec-committees" aria-labelledby="mgec-committees-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="mgec-committees-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Committees</h2></div>
    </div>

    <p class="mgec-lead">Every committee the community elected, most recent first. A year beside a name is the year that member's term ran to. $(member_count) people served across $(term_count) terms.</p>

    <div class="mgec-terms">$(committee_entries)</div>
  </section>

  <section id="mgec-documents" aria-labelledby="mgec-documents-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="mgec-documents-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Documents</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-table-scroll">
      <table class="mgdb-table mgec-doc-table">
        <caption class="mgdb-visually-hidden">Documents of interest produced by or for the MGEC</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Document</th><th scope="col">Format</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>$(document_rows)</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="mgdb-note mgec-note"><strong>Data note:</strong> every link here was checked on 5 September 2026. Six entries across this page have lost their target &#8212; three National Corn Growers Association presentations, the Maize Research Blog, and the 2016 and 2017 community survey reports. Those keep their titles and lose their links, so the record still says the document existed.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="mgec-related" class="mgdb-hub-related" aria-labelledby="mgec-related-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="mgec-related-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Related resources</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-resource-panel">
      <div class="mgdb-resource-list">
        <a href="/maize_history">
          <strong>Maize genetics community history</strong>
          <span>The century of cooperation this committee grew out of, and the meetings and organizations around it</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.maizegenetics.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <strong>Maize Genetics Cooperation</strong>
          <span>The 501&#40;c&#41;&#40;3&#41; the MGEC established in 2019, and where current business is conducted</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/maize_meeting">
          <strong>Maize Genetics Meeting</strong>
          <span>The annual meeting where the committee reported, with its past programs and archived websites</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/mnl">
          <strong>Maize Genetics Cooperation Newsletter</strong>
          <span>Every issue since 1929, including the number 75 essay that set out the committee's mission</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://maizecoopsc.org/about" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <strong>Maize Genetics COOP Stock Center</strong>
          <span>Marty Sachs's extended history of the Cooperation and of the Stock Center</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
)
